{"type":"standard","title":"Lule Sámi","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Lule Sámi</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q56322","titles":{"canonical":"Lule_Sámi","normalized":"Lule Sámi","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Lule Sámi</span></span>"},"pageid":2015852,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Lule-SamiLanguageLocatorMap.svg/330px-Lule-SamiLanguageLocatorMap.svg.png","width":330,"height":217},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Lule-SamiLanguageLocatorMap.svg/960px-Lule-SamiLanguageLocatorMap.svg.png","width":946,"height":622},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1353822504","tid":"c45131e9-4e19-11f1-8d10-b3bb8d8b5ee0","timestamp":"2026-05-12T15:46:40Z","description":"Endangered Uralic language of Scandinavia","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lule_S%C3%A1mi","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lule_S%C3%A1mi?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lule_S%C3%A1mi?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Lule_S%C3%A1mi"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lule_S%C3%A1mi","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Lule_S%C3%A1mi","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lule_S%C3%A1mi?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Lule_S%C3%A1mi"}},"extract":"Lule Sámi is a Uralic-Sámi language spoken around the Lule River in Sweden and in the northern parts of Nordland county in Norway. In Norway it is especially seen in Hamarøy Municipality, where Lule Sámi is one of the official languages. It is written in the Latin script, having an official alphabet.","extract_html":"<p><b>Lule Sámi</b> is a Uralic-Sámi language spoken around the Lule River in Sweden and in the northern parts of Nordland county in Norway. In Norway it is especially seen in Hamarøy Municipality, where Lule Sámi is one of the official languages. It is written in the Latin script, having an official alphabet.</p>"}